            <div xml:id="d384">

                <pb facs="0564" n="490" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg490"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Williams to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 23]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Peking,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-01-31"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 31, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have just been informed by Mr. Vlangaly, the Russian minister, that the Chinese
                    government has extended to Russian ships trading between its open ports and the
                    Russian possessions on the Amoor the same privileges in respect to the payment
                    of tonnage dues that have been granted to vessels trading to Japan and Saigon,
                    as mentioned in my despatch (No. 8) of October 5, 1860. The same privilege
                    enures to American as well as other vessels trading between China and the
                    Amoor.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S. WELLS WILLIAMS, <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé
                        d’Affaires.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
